      "content": "That sounds like you're saying the Court has basically decided that modern problems shouldn't be solved with modern laws if they don't fit a 1700s model. If the historical test \"effectively shields\" rights from almost all modern legislation, isn't it fair to say the legal debate is basically over and the Second Amendment is now an absolute right that outweighs public interest?",
